@title PCSA00015 campaign race - boot to a LIVE RACE on the campaign's first event
@game  PCSA00015

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
#   boot -> attract demo -> PRESS ANY BUTTON -> GAME MODE
#        -> SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN -> campaign intro -> the campaign MAP
#        -> the event EMPIRE CLIMB -> briefing -> START -> the load
#        -> the pre-race RACE card -> the race is LIVE at f9600.
#
# At the end of this recipe the title is racing: LAP 1/3, POS 8/8, the ship on
# the start line at Empire Climb, the world pass carrying several hundred draws.
# ZERO shader fallbacks over the whole run.
#
# >>> IT NEEDS `VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0`, AND THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL.
# With the default per-flip clock top-up a displayed frame carries about a
# TENTH of the guest work a console frame carries, and this title never
# finishes loading at all. See `VitaState::advance_time_frame`.
#
#   VITASLOP_GXP_LIVE=1 VITASLOP_HEADLESS_FRAMES=10000 \
#   VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY=200 VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_FROM=9400 \
#   vitaslop-desktop --game <wipeout>/extracted --recipe <this> --headless <dir>
#
# >>> RETIMED 2026-08-19b, EVERY FRAME MEASURED ON THE CURRENT CLOCK.
# The committed version reached the title screen at f1300; the derived guest
# clock has moved since and it now arrives at ~f5200. Do not scale these by
# hand if the clock moves again - re-measure with `VITASLOP_HEADLESS_SHOT_EVERY`
# and look at the shots.
#   f5100  the attract demo (loading reaches 99% about f5035)
#   f5200  title, PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START
#   f5750  GAME MODE, four tiles
#   f6000  campaign intro ("It's the year 2048...")
#   f6700  the campaign MAP, A.G.R.C 2048, first node captioned TOUCH TO START
#   f8000  EMPIRE CLIMB briefing (PASS: FINISH THE EVENT, NO WEAPONS)
#   f8800  the CONTROLS/RACER legend with LOADING 38%
#   f9200  the pre-race RACE card over a flyby of the circuit
#   f9600  THE RACE IS LIVE
# Judge a live race by the HUD (LAP/POS/TOTAL), never by a world scene: the
# flyby that plays over the load is a world scene and reads exactly like one.
#
# >>> THE TITLE SCREEN WANTS A BUTTON, NOT A TOUCH. The old recipe sent one
# cross and then a touch, which worked when boot went straight to the title
# screen; the attract demo now sits in between, so the first cross dismisses
# that and the title screen needs its own.
#
# >>> THE MAP NEEDS ONE AIMED TAP NOW, NOT TWO BLIND ONES. The old header said
# the map "renders as a white hex lattice, and that is a KNOWN DEFECT" so its
# node could not be aimed at. That defect is FIXED (it was our depth map, not
# the map shader - see `vitaslop-viewport-carries-the-depth-map`), the map draws
# its nodes, and the tap below is read off the shot.
#
# >>> THE GESTURE TYPE MASK MATTERS AND THE DEFAULT IS NOW RIGHT
# SceSystemGesture recognizers come in types 1/2/4/8 and their meanings are not
# published. Reporting a touch to ALL of them tells the title a tap and a drag
# and a pinch happened at once, and the map then only ever PANS - no tap
# selects anything. Type 1 alone selects. `vita::gesture::type_mask` now
# defaults to 1 for that reason; `VITASLOP_GESTURE_TYPE_MASK=15` reproduces the
# old behaviour and this recipe then reaches the map and stops there.
#
# TOUCH COORDINATES are in PANEL coordinates, which are screen*2.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# No input while it loads - this is boot.recipe's ladder, unchanged.

5150: cross
5170:
# Dismisses the attract demo. The title screen is up from about f5200.

5450: cross
5450: @shot title-screen
5470:
# "PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START" -> GAME MODE, up by about f5750.

5800: touch=472,524
5800: @shot game-mode
5840:
# The SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN tile (screen 236,262). ONLINE CAMPAIGN and
# CROSS-PLAY are correctly greyed out (signed out); ADHOC needs a second unit.

6300: touch=1764,960
6300: @shot campaign-intro
6340:
# The intro text ("Touch the nodes to play events") and its confirm checkmark,
# bottom right (screen 882,480).

6800: @section campaign-map
6800: @shot campaign-map

7000: touch=1016,570
7040:
# The first event node (screen 508,285), the only unlocked one. The title
# spawns its LoadingScreenThread a few frames later
# (`VITASLOP_LOG=vitaslop::thread=debug`), which is the machine-readable signal.

8000: @shot event-briefing
# EMPIRE CLIMB / NO WEAPONS, with the track photo, a ship button, a cancel X
# and a START triangle along the bottom (screen 622/752/883, 480).

8400: touch=1766,960
8440:
# START.

8800: @section event-loading
8800: @shot event-loading
# The CONTROLS/RACER legend with a LOADING percentage. That legend is where the
# race controls below come from: STEER/PITCH = LEFT STICK, R = THRUST,
# X = FIRE/USE PICKUP, plus airbrake and absorb.

9200: @shot pre-race
# The RACE card over a flyby of the circuit, with a confirm checkmark.

9400: touch=1762,960
9440:

9600: @section race
9600: @shot race-start
# From here the title is in the event: the HUD reads LAP 1/3 POS 8/8, `start`
# opens the in-race GAME PAUSED menu, and the frame is a race frame - a
# 1024x1024 shadow pass, reflection and post targets, and a world pass of
# several hundred draws into an offscreen target that the composite samples.
#
# @note The composite CANNOT be reproduced by the software renderer: its
# fullscreen blit carries no texcoord attribute (the shader derives the UV), so
# `play`'s `@shot` here is the HUD over black - which is exactly what makes it
# the right oracle for LAP/POS/TOTAL. For the world, render through
# `vitaslop-desktop --headless` with VITASLOP_GXP_LIVE=1.
#
# @todo Drive it, and drive it WELL. `working-area/drive_ai.py` now gets the ship
# @todo round the WHOLE circuit with zero wedges - (296,1215) -> (1224,1108) ->
# @todo (165,643) -> (-414,493) -> (-1291,999) - where every earlier controller
# @todo died against the wall at (1115,1788) inside forty ticks. Three things did
# @todo that, all measured: a speed TARGET instead of a brake on/off switch
# @todo (there are three pedal positions, and it was using two); REFUSING to steer
# @todo at a breadcrumb line shorter than 8 points, because the pack leaves view
# @todo in five ticks and a three-point stub aims sideways into the wall; and
# @todo CARRYING a course, because a heading-holding controller cannot tell a wall
# @todo bounce from a corner and the HUD read WRONG WAY! at 2.50.18.
# @todo STILL NOT COUNTED A LAP. Judge it by the HUD - `ctl shot` renders
# @todo HUD-over-black by design and LAP / POS / TOTAL / shield are all legible -
# @todo never by distance travelled. There is no @assert here until a lap counts.
14000: @section end
